{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790179951,"nonce":"B5HEv46tWlqrMtAovnXFimICLPU=","message":"Reshaped 2026-09-23 (Luis: unify). No iteration namespace, no iteration entity, no iteration value kind. An iteration is an issue of type iteration in refs/work-issues. This task is now schema work: (1) a types attribute on field entities (the type ids a field applies to, empty = all) enforced on write, so start/end dates (roles start, end) and capacity (number) apply to iteration; (2) a target_types attribute on relation entities, enforced on write, so the membership relation (cardinality one) only targets iterations, the same constraint allowed_parents is from the type's side; (3) the views preset excludes type iteration by default; (4) the closing flow keeps the recoverable order: create next, move issues, close old (N+1 commits, idempotent). Further container types (quarter, PI) are more types, not namespaces. See configurable-schema.md D5 (revised) and decision 483dbe2.","files":null}]}